At the foot of Le Morne Brabant, near the public beach, the Slave Route Monument honours the maroons who escaped slavery and sought refuge on the mountain, and all those enslaved in Mauritius.

The memorial bears lines from the poem *Le Morne Territoire Marron* by Richard Sedley Assonne, in memory of those who, according to tradition, "chose the kiss of death over the chains of slavery".

The monument is part of the Le Morne Cultural Landscape, a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 2008. On 1 February, the anniversary of the abolition of slavery in Mauritius, commemorations are held at Le Morne.

## Good to know

- This is a place of remembrance, not a photo backdrop: please behave accordingly.
